{
  "text": " By pushing these vaccines, what's happened is we've put evolutionary pressures on the virus. We always had about six or more different strains of the virus. What happened in Nissen showed this in a paper from Mayo Clinic. We get to 25% of the population vaccinated. That puts an evolutionary pressure on the virus. And the virus that can best survive in the vaccinated emerges forward to be the dominant variant. So by fooling with mother nature, we're getting burned. We've actually extended the problem and made it worse through mass vaccination. Here's the reason why. The spike protein, which is the target of all vaccines, has mutated. Vencrotic Krishnan has shown us now there's antigenic escape. The antibody is the big dark blob on top. The spike protein is the light gray. The spike protein just changed its configuration enough with those mutations. The antibodies can't hit it and certainly can't hit it well enough. It can't be more straightforward. So we have a problem with Delta. For the first time, we have 99% Delta as a single strain in the United States. We've never had that. We always have a blend, just like we have some people of different hair color, different looks and shapes here in the room. Can you imagine? We have a virus now that is completely monotonic. Why do we have 99% Delta? Answer because Delta is thriving in the nose and mouth of those who are vaccinated, thriving. Delta is thriving in the vaccinated. This is the first paper that actually said, do you protect somebody when you take the vaccine? And the answer is, with Delta on the right, you basically, after about four months with Pfizer, you're down to about 10% protection. With AstraZeneca, you're down to zero protection against the person who took the vaccine. And then the unvaccinated contact, there is still some modest protection, modest for someone who took the vaccine. I'm telling you, it's not anything to write home from. The vaccine performance is failing and it's failing substantially.",
